<title>USA: U.S. retailers laid off 980 in Nov - Challenger.</title>
<headline>U.S. retailers laid off 980 in Nov - Challenger.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. retailers announced 980 job cuts in November, down 84 percent from the same month in 1995, according to a report by Challenger, Gray &amp; Christmas.</p>
<p>The report said 6,143 retail employees lost their jobs in November of last year.</p>
<p>&quot;If job cuts mean anything, retailers are doing much better this year than last,&quot; the report said.</p>
<p>Because of store closings last year, fewer retail outlets are operating this holiday season, it said.</p>
<p>--N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660</p>
